# AGENTS.md

Project guidelines for AI assistants.

## ⚠️ MANDATORY: Always Use Git — Never Local-Only Changes

**Every code change must go through Git. No exceptions.**

1. **Bugs** → Create an Issue
2. **Triage** → Apply labels
3. **Code changes** → Always create a branch, commit, and open a PR. Never edit files directly on main.
4. **Review** → All PRs must pass the Reviewer quality gate
5. **Resolve** → Close the Issue via PR merge

### Workflow for every change:
```
1. Create Issue → 2. Create branch → 3. Delegate to team → 4. Commit & push
5. Open PR → 6. Review → 7. Merge (auto-closes issue)
```

## Autonomous Agent Organization

This project has an **autonomous agent organization** at `.agents/` with:
- **{{roleCount}} specialized agents** across {{teamCount}} teams + dispatcher + reviewer{{#if hasSecurityOfficer}} + security officer{{/if}} + tech lead
- **Full CI/CD pipeline** — lint → test → security → build → deploy
- **Git-first bug tracking** — all bugs as Issues with labels
- **Separation of powers** — no agent can both write and approve code
- **Personal memory** — each agent has persistent context across sessions

**Read the full organization**: `.agents/ORGANIZATION.md`

### Quick Commands
```bash
# Report a bug
gh issue create --title "bug title" --body "description" --label "type:bug,severity:medium"

# Triage
gh issue edit <number> --add-label "team:backend,priority:high"

# Create a branch for a fix
git checkout -b fix/issue-<number>-<short-description>

# Commit and push
git add -A && git commit -m "fix(scope): description closes #<number>"
git push origin fix/issue-<number>-<short-description>

# Open PR
gh pr create --title "fix(scope): description" --body "Closes #<number>" --label "team:backend"

# Review a PR
gh pr review <number>

# Check CI
gh pr checks <number>

# Merge
gh pr merge <number> --squash
```

